---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const ld = [{ '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'Organization', name: SITE.publisherName, url: SITE.domain, email: SITE.contactEmail }];
---
<Page title="About FBA Tactics" eyebrow="About" description="Who publishes FBA Tactics, what the site covers, how its pages are researched and checked, and how it is funded." lede="A reference site for people who import goods into the United States and sell them on online marketplaces." jsonld={ld}>
  <h2 id="who">Who publishes this site</h2>
  <p>FBA Tactics is published by <strong>{SITE.publisherName}</strong>{SITE.editorName && <> and edited by <strong>{SITE.editorName}</strong></>}. The site went online in {SITE.foundedYear}. You can reach the publisher at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
  {SITE.editorBio && <p>{SITE.editorBio}</p>}
  <h2>What the site covers</h2>
  <p>The name dates from the site's start as a guide for sellers using Fulfillment by Amazon. Since November 2026 the focus is narrower and more checkable: the published fees of the major US marketplaces, and the federal import rules that apply before those goods are listed.</p>
  <p>Two things that decide whether an imported product makes money on a marketplace: the fees each platform charges, and the US customs rules that apply between the factory and the warehouse. The guides cover entry types, customs bonds, classification, country of origin and marking, valuation, additional duties, drawback, foreign-trade zones, product certificates, hazardous materials in shipping, the federal rule on consumer reviews, and the inventory accounting the IRS expects. The fee reference pages cover Amazon, Walmart, eBay, Etsy and Shopify.</p>
  <h2>Where the information comes from</h2>
  <p>Only from the body that issues the rule or the fee: the Code of Federal Regulations, Federal Register notices, IRS publications, and each marketplace's own public fee pages. Every fact on a page carries a numbered link to that source and the date it was checked. We do not cite blogs, vendors, forums or other summaries, and if a figure cannot be traced to a primary source that a reader can open, it is not published. The full rules are on the <a href="/editorial-standards/">editorial and sourcing policy</a> page.</p>
  <h2>How pages are produced</h2>
  <p>Pages are researched and drafted with the help of AI writing tools working from the primary sources listed on each page. A separate checking pass then reopens every cited source and compares it with the sentence it supports; any statement the source does not support is corrected or removed. Before a page is published, a named reviewer for the publisher reads it against its sources, and the reviewer's name and the review date appear under the headline. The site's build refuses to publish a page without that record. Every figure is recorded in a claims register with its source, the date it was checked, and its status. The publisher is responsible for everything on the site. When a figure changes or an error is found, the change is logged on the <a href="/corrections/">corrections page</a>.</p>
  <p>Nobody on this site claims to have tested products or services, and the site does not publish reviews of software, suppliers or service providers.</p>
  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p>The site is intended to be funded by display advertising served by Google AdSense. Advertisers do not choose, review or influence content, ads are labeled "Advertisement", and they are never placed inside tables, calculators, navigation or source lists. There are no sponsored posts, affiliate links or paid placements. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for what advertising means for your data.</p>
  <h2>What this site is not</h2>
  <p>It is not legal, tax or customs advice, and it is not affiliated with any marketplace or government agency. For a decision about your specific goods, the routes are a binding ruling from US Customs and Border Protection, a licensed customs broker, or a tax professional. See the <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>.</p>
</Page>
